# Port Plan — Step 08: The REPL Loop (Ruby → Python)

Port `Boukensha::Repl` — the interactive session loop — plus `Boukensha.repl`,
a `VERSION` constant, and the three supporting changes that make conversation
history actually accumulate.

This is the ninth of thirteen steps (`00_config` → `12_context`).

> **The step's real subject is memory, not the loop.** A REPL that forgot its own
> replies would be useless, and up to step 07 the agent never put its final text
> into the Context — it returned it and dropped it. `agent.rb` gains three
> `add_message(:assistant, …)` calls, and that is what makes the REPL work.

